Description: build the binary into obj/ where the packaging class expects it
 The project sets TARGET_DIR=.. so a developer build drops the binary next
 to the themes/ directory at the project root. The vos_makefile_engine
 packaging class installs obj/<NAME> to /system/apps/<NAME> (and compiles
 the catalogs under obj/), so a binary at the project root cannot be
 packaged: dh_auto_install would look for obj/BeMines and fail. Drop the
 line: the engine already defaults TARGET_DIR to OBJ_DIR when it is unset,
 which is the layout every other class-1 port uses. The package still ships
 themes/ beside the installed binary (debian/bemines.install), which is
 where the app scans for them at runtime.
Author: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: no
Origin: https://github.com/HaikuArchives/BeMines
--- a/src/Makefile
+++ b/src/Makefile
@@ -6,7 +6,6 @@
 
 # The name of the binary.
 NAME = BeMines
-TARGET_DIR = ..
 
 # The type of binary, must be one of:
 #	APP:	Application
